# Per-user per-remote rclone secrets — one file per remote per user.
# Copy this file to "./secrets/alice-gdrive" and fill in real values.
# The filename suffix after "<user>-" IS the rclone remote name (env-safe:
# letters, digits, underscore only — no '-' or other characters).
# KEY=VAL lines; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# SRC_DIR / TGT_DIR map to ALICE_SRC_DIR / ALICE_TGT_DIR.
# Every other key maps to RCLONE_CONFIG_<REMOTE>_<KEY> (the rclone remote).
# RCLONE_OPTS holds extra rclone flags (per-remote), e.g.
# RCLONE_OPTS=--fast-list --drive-chunk-size 64M.
# CRON overrides ALICE_CRON for just this remote (default: the per-user
# schedule). ENABLED=0/false removes this remote's crontab entry without
# deleting the file (falsy: 0|false, case-insensitive; absent = enabled).
# CRON="0 3 * * *"
# ENABLED=1
TYPE=drive
CLIENT_ID=
CLIENT_SECRET=
TOKEN=
SCOPE=drive
SRC_DIR=/synctarget/alice
TGT_DIR=gdrive:/Backups
# RCLONE_OPTS=--fast-list --drive-chunk-size 64M
#
# Optional rclone drive options (uncomment as needed):
# ROOT_FOLDER_ID=
# SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=
# TEAM_DRIVE=
